# Spot Fleet Data Lake — Orbit API-Based Design

> Source of truth: **Boston Dynamics Orbit** (formerly Scout) — the fleet data
> centralization platform. Orbit collects, organizes, and stores data from
> every mission and teleoperation session executed by the Spot fleet. The lake
> consumes it via the **Orbit Web API**: REST over HTTPS, `Bearer`-token auth,
> all resources under `/api/v0/`.
>
> References:
> - Spot SDK repo: https://github.com/boston-dynamics/spot-sdk (v5.1.9)
> - Orbit API docs: `docs/concepts/orbit/orbit_api.md` in the repo
> - `bosdyn-orbit` Python package: `python/bosdyn-orbit/src/bosdyn/orbit/`
> - Full OAS3 spec: your Orbit instance's API reference
>   (`docs/orbit/docs` on dev.bostondynamics.com)

---

## 1. What data Spot produces (SDK-side inventory)

Every Python client under `bosdyn/client/` maps to a **gRPC service running on
the robot**. These services are the ultimate producers of the data Orbit
aggregates. Understanding them tells you what content to expect in runs,
captures, and run logs.

| Domain | SDK source | Data shape | Rate/volume |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Telemetry / robot state** | `robot_state.py` | Protobuf: joint states, kinematics, foot contacts, battery, power state, behavior faults, E-stop | ~15 Hz on the robot; lands in Orbit per-run via run logs |
| **Imagery** | `image.py`, `spot_cam/`, `gripper_camera_param.py` | 5 fisheye grayscale + front stereo color; Spot CAM adds PTZ; JPEG/PNG + proto metadata | On demand (heavy: MB/frame) |
| **Point clouds / LIDAR** | `point_cloud.py`, `local_grid.py` | EAP LIDAR point clouds; terrain/obstacle local grids | On demand |
| **World objects** | `world_object.py` | Fiducials (AprilTags), detected objects, door handles — 3D pose + frame transforms | Per request |
| **Logs & BDDF** | `bddf.py`, `bddf_download.py`, `recording.py`, `log_status.py` | **BDDF** (Boston Dynamics Data Format) — black-box recorder: signals, comments, faults; `.walk` recordings | Batch offload |
| **Autonomy / maps** | `graph_nav.py`, `autowalk.py`, `map_processing.py` | `.walk` folders (graph maps, anchoring, point clouds), mission state, AutoWalk programs | Per mapping/mission |
| **Data Acquisition (payloads)** | `data_acquisition.py`, `data_acquisition_store.py`, `data_acquisition_plugin.py` | Payload sensor captures (thermal, gas, PTZ — anything plugged into Spot) | Per capture request |
| **Health & faults** | `spot_check.py`, `fault.py`, `metrics_logging.py` | Diagnostics, service faults, metrics RPCs | On demand / event |
| **Fleet admin** | `robot_id.py`, `payload.py`, `license.py` | Robot serial, nickname, firmware, payload registry, software versions | Slow-changing reference |
| **Time sync** | `time_sync.py` | Robot clock ↔ client clock offsets | Every session (robot-direct only) |

Orbit sits on top of all of this: the robots upload mission runs, captures,
and logs to Orbit, and you consume the already-centralized result via REST.

