## 4. Design decisions

### 4.1 The Run is the partition key
Not robot/time — `run_uuid` is Orbit's organizing unit. Bronze tables partition
by `dt` (run start date) for query pruning, but every row carries `run_uuid`,
plus `robot`, `mission_name`, and `site_walk_uuid` as columns. The dominant
query patterns are "everything from run X" and "all runs of mission Y on robot
Z this month".

### 4.2 Two ingest modes
- **Incremental polling** — `GET /runs?started_at>watermark`, then fetch child
  RunEvents / RunCaptures / run log. Watermarks live in `_meta/ingestion/`.
- **Bulk backfill** — `GET /run_archives/{runId}` yields each run's complete
  zip. Use to seed history and to re-derive anything mishandled downstream.
  Keep zips in `00-landing/` untouched.

### 4.3 Webhooks make it near-real-time
Register a webhook (`POST /webhooks`) for new runs / completions. The listener
appends the raw callback body to `00-landing/webhooks_events/` **first**
(always keep the raw record), then triggers an incremental pull for that
`run_uuid`. Webhooks are hints, not guarantees — keep the periodic poller as
reconciliation.

### 4.4 Anomalies are first-class
This is the resource SDK-direct users don't get: human/algorithm-reviewed
findings attached to inspection data (e.g. "thermal hotspot at gauge 3").
Ingest it into bronze, promote to `03-gold/anomaly_pipeline/`. Note the write
path: `PATCH /anomalies` (bulk close by element IDs, or patch by uuid) lets a
downstream review UI triage/close anomalies directly against Orbit.

### 4.5 Run Statistics + Facets = instant Gold
BD pre-computes session statistics (`/run_statistics/sessions`,
`/sessions_summary`) and per-mission run counts (`/runs/facets/missions`).
Seed `03-gold/` from these on day one so dashboards work immediately; treat
the lake's own silver-derived aggregations as eventually authoritative.
Disagreement between the two is a built-in data-quality check.

### 4.6 Run logs replace live robot_state streaming
Robot-direct streaming (15 Hz `robot_state`, time sync) is gone; each run's
log arrives post-hoc. Silver `telemetry/` is therefore **per-run**, not
continuous. If live telemetry is needed later, re-add a robot-direct SDK
side-car as an adjacent `ingest-spot-sdk/` tree (keep raw BDDF + protobuf
bytes there, pin `protos/bosdyn/api/` per SDK version in `_meta/schemas/`).
The lake layout above doesn't change.

### 4.7 Pin the OpenAPI spec
The OAS3 document is versioned (`5.0.0` at time of writing) and bronze schemas
derive from it. Keep pinned copies in `_meta/schemas/` and stamp
`orbit_version` / `api_version` columns on every table so a multi-instance or
